## Notes (workers report problems here; the planner's decisions so far)
- Roof zone: `mcd roof` removes everything at y>=8 within x=-2..18, z=8..22 and rebuilds the house roof. Nothing but the house may stand at y>=8 there (porch roof tops out at y=7 on purpose; the shell must not exceed y=7).
- `make.sh` skips the roof step while the shell is absent (stubs). Once P1 exists it dry-runs then builds the roof from roof.json (cottage preset, pitch 45, red-tile, chimney `at [9,14]` = cells x9..10, z14..15). If a roof warning appears, read it; do not use bypass flags.
- `vocab.mjs` `fixConnections` runs after all parts and rewrites fences/walls/panes/bars with correct connections: place them without states.
- `test-vocab.mjs` renders every helper (`node test-vocab.mjs`, then `mcd render /tmp/farm-vocab.nbt`); shutters and door facing were checked there (shutters lie flat on the wall, doors read from outside).
- Water: every water cell must be enclosed on its sides and underside by non-air; the beds' pools sit in farmland, the well in its ring. Do not add water anywhere else.
- P1 (shell): the jamb/lintel pass only frames house-wall openings (x1..15, z11..19); the greenhouse and shed doors are not framed by P1 (their parts own those walls). The upper windows (y=7, h=1) get jambs only: their lintel would sit at y=8 in the roof zone, so it is skipped. Chimney breast is bricks x9..10 z14..15 y2..7; the hearth niche (10,2..3,15) is unset.
- Trees from `tree()` and leaf blocks: oak_leaves has no state in this version, so just place the block.
----
BUILD: farmhouse-crew: a farmhouse with a potager garden, the French-country kitchen garden kind. Recognisable elements: a two-storey farmhouse of rough stone with a steep pitched roof, a brick chimney, shuttered windows, a timber porch or lean-to on the garden side; beside it the potager: a walled or fenced rectangular garden laid out symmetrically, with raised beds edged in timber or brick, gravel or brick paths crossing at a centre feature (a well, sundial or urn), rows of different crops in each bed (wheat, carrots, potatoes, beetroot), fruit trees trained against the wall, a small cold frame or greenhouse, a tool shed, a rose or bean arch over the main path; lanterns and a gate from the house to the garden.
SIZE: about 40 wide (front, x), 36 deep, 14 tall to the chimney top; 1:1 scale, a player is 2 blocks tall.
----
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# The ONE command that makes build.nbt from scratch: generator parts -> house roof (mcd roof, cottage preset) -> build.nbt.
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(dirname "$0")"
MCD="node /Volumes/ext1/swe/repos/minecraft-design/tools/bin/mcd.mjs"
node build.mjs build.raw.nbt
# The roof step only makes sense once the shell exists (the stubs leave bare ground): look for the front door lintel wall.
if node --input-type=module -e '
  import { load } from "/Volumes/ext1/swe/repos/minecraft-design/tools/src/build.mjs";
  const g = load("build.raw.nbt"); process.exit(g.isAir(1, 7, 11) ? 1 : 0);'; then
  # cottage preset (house -> cottage): 45-degree pitch keeps the ridge at y=12; red-tile reads against the grey stone; 2x2 brick chimney at x=9..10,z=14..15
  $MCD roof build.raw.nbt --spec roof.json --dry-run
  $MCD roof build.raw.nbt build.tmp.nbt --spec roof.json
  mv build.tmp.nbt build.nbt
else
  echo "no house shell yet: skipping the roof step (bare ground)"
  cp build.raw.nbt build.nbt
fi
$MCD info build.nbt | head -8
----
// Farmhouse + potager generator: `node build.mjs [out.nbt]` (default build.raw.nbt). make.sh adds the house roof afterwards.
import { Grid, runParts, SIZE, fixConnections } from "./vocab.mjs";
import * as shell from "./parts/shell.mjs";
import * as porch from "./parts/porch.mjs";
import * as potager from "./parts/potager.mjs";
import * as features from "./parts/features.mjs";
import * as interior from "./parts/interior.mjs";
import * as grounds from "./parts/grounds.mjs";
import { renameSync } from "node:fs";
import { dirname, join } from "node:path";
import { fileURLToPath } from "node:url";

const here = dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));
const out = process.argv[2] ?? join(here, "build.raw.nbt");
const g = new Grid(SIZE);
// the ground: grass at y=0 over the whole site (cells set here stay writable by every part: paths and farmland may replace it)
g.fill([0, 0, 0], [SIZE[0] - 1, 0, SIZE[2] - 1], "grass_block");
const reports = runParts(g, [
  ["house shell", shell.build],
  ["porch + openings", porch.build],
  ["potager", potager.build],
  ["garden features", features.build],
  ["interior", interior.build],
  ["grounds", grounds.build],
], { palette: join(here, "palette.json") });
console.log("connections fixed:", fixConnections(g));
const tmp = out + ".tmp.nbt";
g.save(tmp);
renameSync(tmp, out);
console.log(JSON.stringify({ saved: out, size: g.size, parts: reports.map((r) => `${r.part}:${r.placed}${r.refused ? `(refused ${r.refused})` : ""}`) }));

